The run is failing due to a **patch naming/topology mismatch** between mesh generation and `0/` field files, plus an inlet creation issue.

- `log.pimpleFoam`: `Cannot find patchField entry for bottom` means your mesh has a `bottom` patch (from `system/blockMeshDict`) but `0/p` (and likely `0/U`) still define `base` instead of `bottom`.
- `log.createPatch`: `Face 88 ... is not an external face` means `topoSet` selected at least one internal face, and `createPatch` can only repatch boundary faces.

What to fix (without changing required physics/setup values):

- In all initial fields (`0/U`, `0/p`, and any other `0/*` using boundary sections), make boundary names exactly match mesh patches from `blockMeshDict`: `bottom`, `top`, `sides`, `frontAndBack`, and new `inlet` after `createPatch`.
